---
description: Project coding guidelines
alwaysApply: true
---
- no explicit any or as unknown
- in dynamic or inline imports, all imports must be declared at the top of the file
- Create an index.ts for each feature and component for all exports, do not re-export imports
- Create a types.ts for each feature and component for all types and interfaces rather than using inline definitions
- Explicitly define interfaces
- type definitions belong in types.ts
- use Zod validation types in shared/schema for any objects shared between the frontend and backend
- do not include z or manipulate Zod types in the backend or frontend apps, all Zod type manipulation must be in shared/schema
- Use camelCase for all variable and prop names.
- Prefix unused variables with _
- React components must have strictly typed props
- Use Tailwind + base-ui for styling

Organize imports in the following order:
1. Built-in Node.js modules
2. External packages (e.g., React, lodash, express, cors)
3. Aliased/internal packages (e.g., @shared/schema, @shared/prisma-client, @/lib/foo)
4. Parent imports (e.g., ../foo)
5. Sibling imports (e.g., ./bar)
6. Index imports (e.g., ./)

- Separate each group with a blank line.
- Within each group, sort imports alphabetically (case-insensitive).
- Do not add empty lines within a group.
- Imports starting with @shared/ or @/ are considered internal/aliased and should come after external packages but before parent/sibling/index imports.
- Alphabetize alias imports with respect to each other and with other internal imports.
- Type-only imports follow the same order and grouping as value imports.
